{"base_rate":0.16890080428954424,"brier":0.09823525469168902,"bss":0.30018572708653335,"bss_hi":0.40057175894865127,"bss_lo":0.18179977603314978,"country":"ES","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07274798927613943,"ess":292.68545874876145,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Malaga</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Malaga rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (96%), believe about\n<b>75%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 746 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMALAGA AEROPUERTO, 8.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.30, ranked 60 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(35&ndash;93) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>432</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>17%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'><b>39%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Malaga</b> <span class=\"muted\">ES</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.30</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>35&ndash;93\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>746 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Malaga &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Malaga\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 71.61858823529411,352.0235294117647 118.67923076923077,288.6666666666667 264.40560000000005,134.48 398.8647368421053,18.0 398.8647368421053,46.73684210526318 264.40560000000005,207.28 118.67923076923077,349.3333333333333 71.61858823529411,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"320.5201072386059\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"320.5201072386059\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,368.51851851851853 71.61858823529411,339.1764705882353 118.67923076923077,316.6666666666667 264.40560000000005,241.25333333333333 398.8647368421053,109.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 432 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"368.51851851851853\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 85 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"71.61858823529411\" cy=\"339.1764705882353\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 17%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"118.67923076923077\" cy=\"316.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 58%&amp;#10;It rained 39% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"264.40560000000005\" cy=\"241.25333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"398.8647368421053\" cy=\"109.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(17%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Malaga the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.32) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.10).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>183</td><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'>-0.098</td><td class='num'>1.5%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.204</td><td class='num'>13.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'>0.294</td><td class='num'>5.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>211</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.320</td><td class='num'>7.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":36.72016,"lon":-4.42034,"n":746,"n_cities":109,"name":"Malaga","offset_days":1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":432,"obs":0.037037037037037035,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03847058823529411,"n":85,"obs":0.11764705882352941,"sig":true},{"hi":0.33,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.17141025641025642,"n":78,"obs":0.1794871794871795,"sig":false},{"hi":0.85,"lo":0.33,"mean":0.5830666666666667,"n":75,"obs":0.38666666666666666,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.85,"mean":0.9628947368421054,"n":76,"obs":0.75,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":8.5,"rank":60,"rank_hi":93.0,"rank_lo":34.925000000000004,"reliability":0.010010921639805825,"resolution":0.049549216737934526,"slug":"malaga","station":"MALAGA AEROPUERTO","timezone":"Europe/Madrid"}